course: dictionary
lesson: 3816
title: Forget and its many forms
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Forget is a verb, so its form changes to show when something happens: forget, forgets, forgot, forgotten, forgetting. Forgot is the past, as in «Noah forgot to log out at the library, and his account posted "I LOVE BROCCOLI" in a chat.» Forgotten is used with have or has, as in I have forgotten my lunch.
explain: Forget has three main meanings. First, not to remember something, like a fact, a name or a word. Second, not to remember to do or bring something, like your lunch. Third, to stop thinking about something on purpose, as when you say «Forget it».
explain: Forgetful describes someone who often forgets things. Tricks to stop forgetting include lists, notes and routines, like packing your bag the night before. Forgetting is a normal part of being busy, but it can cause trouble, which is why so many stories start with someone forgetting something.
fact: Forget is a verb: forget, forgets, forgot, forgotten, forgetting.
fact: «Forget» means not to remember, not to remember to do or bring something, or to stop thinking about something on purpose.
fact: «Forgetful» means someone who often forgets things.
fact: Longer words double their last consonant only when the stress falls on the last part: be-GIN becomes beginning, and for-GET becomes forgetting.
fact: Grey squirrels bury nuts in many spots and find many by memory and smell, but the acorns that squirrels and jays forget can grow into new oak trees.
exercise: In «Noah forgot to log out at the library», which word is the past tense of forget? | *forgot | log | library | account
exercise: Which spelling is the correct -ing form of forget? | forgotting | forgeting | *forgetting | forgetiing
exercise: «Don't forget your lunch.» Which meaning of forget is this? | To stop thinking about something on purpose | *Not to remember to bring something | Not to be able to see | Not to remember a name
test: Which sentence uses forget to mean stop thinking about something on purpose? | «Forgetting the spelling cost me marks.» | *«Forget it, it was only a joke.» | «Grey squirrels forget where some nuts are.» | «I forgot my pencil case again.»
test: Which word means someone who often forgets things? | forgiving | forgot | useful | *forgetful
exam: Fill both gaps: Yesterday I ___ my book, and today I have ___ to bring it back. | forgets and forgot | forget and forget | forgot and forgetting | *forgot and forgotten
